  data: {
    LLM: '1. Four cards dealt to each player. 2. Non-dealer cuts for starter card (turn-up). 3. Players alternately play cards to the pile, pegging points for fifteens, pairs, runs during play. 4. After all cards played, hands are counted for combinations. 5. Starter card applies to both hands.',
    Player: '1. Four cards dealt to each player. 2. Non-dealer cuts for starter card (turn-up). 3. Players alternately play cards to the pile, pegging points for fifteens, pairs, runs during play. 4. After all cards played, hands are counted for combinations. 5. Starter card applies to both hands.',
    objective: 'Score points through card combinations (fifteens, pairs, runs, flushes) and be first to reach the target score (typically 31 or 61).',
    gameplay: '1. Four cards dealt to each player. 2. Non-dealer cuts for starter card (turn-up). 3. Players alternately play cards to the pile, pegging points for fifteens, pairs, runs during play. 4. After all cards played, hands are counted for combinations. 5. Starter card applies to both hands.',
